{{!
    @template local_awareness/manage/cell_title

    The Title cell: the notice title, with the pages it applies to underneath.

    The stylesheet clamps the title to two lines; the title attribute carries it whole.

    The title arrives already through format_string(), which resolves the text filters and strips
    or cleans the markup, so it is emitted with a triple stash: escaping it again would print its
    entities literally. The path is the opposite case — a URL pattern rather than prose — so it
    arrives raw and is escaped here by Mustache.

    Context variables required:
    * title (string) — the filtered notice title, safe HTML
    * titleplain (string) — the same title for the tooltip attribute
    * where (string) — the raw path pattern, or the "anywhere" sentence
    * course (object, optional) — on the site list, the course a course notice belongs to:
      name (string, already a sentence) and url (string, empty when the course is gone)

    Example context (json):
    {
        "title": "Scheduled maintenance",
        "titleplain": "Scheduled maintenance",
        "where": "/course/view.php%",
        "course": {"name": "Course: Astronomy 101", "url": "https://example.com/course/view.php?id=2"}
    }
}}
<span class="local-awareness-celltitle" title="{{titleplain}}">{{{title}}}</span>
<span class="local-awareness-subline" title="{{where}}">{{where}}</span>
{{#course}}
    <span class="local-awareness-subline local-awareness-scope">
        {{#url}}<a href="{{url}}">{{name}}</a>{{/url}}{{^url}}{{name}}{{/url}}
    </span>
{{/course}}
